// ============================================================================
//  MINIATURE CITY SIMULATION — Unified Sketch
//  Target: Arduino Mega 2560
//
//  Subsystems (all non-blocking, driven from one shared loop() via millis()):
//    - 2x Vehicular + Pedestrian traffic light pairs (Intersection 1 & 2,
//      work inversely — only one is ever GREEN/YELLOW at a time)
//    - City lights (LDR-controlled, hysteresis band, survives a missing LDR)
//    - Train barrier (servo + SPI OLED countdown, survives a missing OLED)
//
//  Pin allocation rule (per project spec):
//    - Pins 2-13  : RESERVED ONLY for PWM-driven elements (traffic yellows,
//                   city lights, buzzers)
//    - Pins 0, 1  : left unused (reserved for Serial/USART0 — required for
//                   debug output and the OLED/LDR fallback warnings)
//    - Pins 14-53 : everything else (solid-state LEDs, servo, OLED control)
//
//  NOTE: Not compiled/verified in this environment (no Arduino toolchain
//  access here) — please compile in the Arduino IDE. Report any errors and
//  I'll fix them immediately.
// ============================================================================

